      "thinking": "I'm trying to recall the exact name Dodson & Hilton used for this son of Ramesses II, wondering if it's Minemaes or some variant like Mentuemwia, since the name doesn't quite match what I'd expect.\n\nI'm not confident \"aes\" maps to a standard word here, which makes me doubt this reading — Dodson & Hilton typically render ms as \"-mose,\" so \"Minemaes\" breaking that pattern is suspicious. I don't have a clear match for this name across the dynasties I'm considering, so I'm leaning on the general rule that vowels can be inserted anywhere in the transliteration.\n\n\"Minmose\" seems the natural spelling, while \"Minemaes\" would require positing an unattested word, which feels like a stretch. I'll settle on C1.\n\n",
